# Spec-driven development (SDD)

CampusHub follows Spec Kit–style SDD.

## Before writing product code

1. Read `.specify/memory/constitution.md`.
2. Read `specs/000-product/spec.md` (baseline + backlog).
3. For a **new slice**, create or update `specs/NNN-slug/spec.md` (copy `.specify/templates/spec-template.md`). Set `.specify/feature.json` `feature_directory` to that folder.
4. Add a short `plan.md` (and `tasks.md` if more than a handful of files).
5. Implement only what the spec requires. Cite `CH-Snn` in new code (see `SddStories`).
6. Add or extend tests with `[Trait("Story", "CH-Snn")]`. Seed mock data so the screens in the spec are clickable.
7. When the user says **proceed to next**, take the next backlog item in `specs/000-product/spec.md`, specify it, then implement — do not invent a slice with no spec.

Story index: `specs/STORIES.md` (BA format: As a / I want / So that). Workflow: `specs/WORKFLOW.md`.

## Commands (Cursor skills)

Use project skills: `speckit-specify`, `speckit-plan`, `speckit-tasks`, `speckit-implement`, `speckit-clarify`, `speckit-converge`.

## Do not

- Implement an undocumented SaaS slice from chat alone
- Commit `.tmp-build/`, `*.db`, `bin/`, `obj/`, `node_modules/`
- Open a new public API port for the student UI
